# Unsure about A1 as a possible bridge on "perceive". In parts_perceived, "must be perceived" means each part exists only as perceived.
# In perceive_innum, "perceive (distinguish)" means being able to discriminate parts one by one.
# A critic might say a part can be perceived as part of the whole without being singled out, which would make A1 a bridge.
# But the text glosses "perceive" as "distinguish" in S2 and treats the two as one, so I read A1 as joining two claims in one sense of the word.
